WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:06.170
"A Midwinter's Tale" is an intriguing standalone
solstice story that also offers a sneak peek

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:10.370
at what we can look forward to in Season 2
of Chilling Adventures of Sabrina.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.370
Spoilers ahead…

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.960
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm breaking down the seven biggest

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.440
Season 2 reveals from A Midwinter's Tale and
explaining what those Three Demon Kings are

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.400
really up to in Greendale!

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.391
Let's begin with Letitia, which we learn is
the name Zelda has given to the baby girl

00:00:26.391 --> 00:00:28.600
that she stole away from Father Blackwood.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.870
At the end of the holiday episode, Zelda explains
that after what happened with Gryla, she feels

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.809
it won't be possible to keep the baby girl
hidden from Blackwood in the Spellman house.

00:00:36.809 --> 00:00:41.170
So, her plan is to take Letitia to Dezmelda
who she says "will raise her in seclusion,

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.850
teaching her the old ways, as is her birthright."

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.629
Dezmelda previously appeared in the Feast
of Feasts episode of season 1.

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:52.170
She's an excommunicated witch who lives alone
in the woods and who Sabrina, Ms Wardwell

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.641
and the Weird Sisters visited when they were
finding out more about the history of the

00:00:55.641 --> 00:00:56.960
Feast of Feasts.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.960
Dezmelda actually has her own history with
the High Priest of the Church of Night, as

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.140
she was selected as the queen for the cannibalistic
feast when she was a child, but she fled for

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.850
her own safety when she learned the high priest
planned to violate her as part of an initiation

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.110
for the ritual.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.290
If Dezmelda is raising a potential challenger
to the all-male hierarchy that Blackwood is

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.299
forming at the Church of Night, it adds some
interest to this future plotline as she may

00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:24.210
use the baby girl as a means of getting revenge
for her past mistreatment by the Church.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:28.630
Remember that Letitia is Blackwood's first-born
and therefore the rightful heir to lead the

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.409
Church over Judas.

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:35.290
However, Blackwood thinks Judas is his only
child after Zelda decided to keep Letitia's

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:39.909
birth a secret from him as she feared for
the baby girl's safety.

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:43.859
Sabrina's mother Diana made a special appearance
in the holiday episode and gave us what seem

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:47.520
to be a few revelations about why she's been
stuck in Limbo.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.640
When Sabrina speaks to her toward the end
of the episode, Diana seems to be saying that

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.899
she was worried about whether Sabrina was
being taken care of.

00:01:54.899 --> 00:01:59.330
Now that Diana can see that Sabrina has a
loving family who watch over her, the implication

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.310
seems to be that she may now be able to pass
on from Limbo.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.890
However, I suspect we will see more of Diana
even if it's only in flashbacks.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:11.720
I also wonder whether there's a chance any
of her appearances were a trick by Ms Wardwell.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:16.010
It's just a possible theory, but when Diana
first appeared during the séance and Sabrina

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.030
asked her about why she was stuck in Limbo,
the message relayed back was "not safe".

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:24.360
I don't know if she was just referring to
the spirits of the Yuletide Lads who were

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.209
invading the Spellman residence or if she
was alluding to something else.

00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:31.880
The other suspicious thing is that the proof
Diana offered up to Sabrina that she really

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.080
was her mum was just her flight number which
is something that could be easily known by

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.910
someone nefarious who conspired to cause the
plane accident or at least knew about it.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.120
Something we also discover is that Diana learned
some spells from her husband Edward which

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.629
is how she taught Sabrina the changeling trick
she performed on Gryla.

00:02:48.629 --> 00:02:53.560
However, Diana warns Sabrina that while she
herself followed Edward down the Path of Night,

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:58.330
she wouldn't recommend that to any other mortals,
which has implications for Brina's relationship

00:02:58.330 --> 00:02:59.740
with Harvey.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.780
At the end of "A Midwinter's Tale", Harvey
gives back to Brina the magic pencils she

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.200
gifted him and he asks her never to use magic
around or on him again.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.220
It's an uncomfortable moment for the pair,
so I'm curious as to how in Season 2 we'll

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.520
see the two of them back together again, given
what we saw teased in the trailer for Part

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:17.520
2?

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.720
And will Sabrina actually keep her tacit agreement
not to use any magic on Harvey again?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.879
One thing we do know that is pretty likely
from the way this episode ends and the teases

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:30.890
from the Season 2 trailer is that we'll be
getting more emphasis on the love triangle

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.300
set up between Sabrina, Nick and Harvey.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.860
Although "A Midwinter's Tale" wraps up quite
nicely, it wouldn't be Chilling Adventures

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.840
of Sabrina without the tease of something
much more sinister for Season 2!

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.681
"Oh and now all we have to do is get through
Witch Epiphany in one piece without, er, some

00:03:46.681 --> 00:03:50.090
other terror rising from the bowels of Hell."

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:54.019
The Witch's Epiphany that Hilda is referring
to is likely the coven's version of the Christian

00:03:54.019 --> 00:03:58.650
feast day of the Epiphany which takes place
on the 6th of January and is also known as

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.910
Three Kings' Day.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:04.680
Although Hilda's semi-joking, it looks like
her fears are being realised as the episode

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:09.340
closes with three demon kings emerging from
the entrance of a Greendale mine.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:13.459
In the traditional story of Christmas, three
kings or wise men travelled to visit Jesus

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:17.299
after his birth, bearing gifts of frankincense,
myrrh and gold.

00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:21.340
The arrival of these three demonic-looking
kings in Greendale could be related to the

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.720
recent birth of Father Blackwood's son Judas
and I wonder if they are bringing gifts from

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.960
Hell or the Devil for the little baby boy?

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.639
Apparently, the title of the Part 2 premiere
will be "The Epiphany" so I imagine we'll

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:34.150
find out then.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:38.500
Another possibility is that the three kings'
arrival is to greet the birth of an antichrist-type

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.500
figure.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.830
It might just be a coincidence, but it's curious
that Nick Scratch was conveniently away visiting

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.960
the "unholy lands" during the episode and
I've talked previously about Nick's possible

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:52.370
darker side as "Old Nick" and "Old Scratch"
are both nicknames for the Devil.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:56.580
The arrival of these three kings may also
be related to an interesting scene which appeared

00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:01.389
in the trailer for the holiday special but
which never actually made it into the episode.

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:05.360
In the trailer, there's a shot of Sabrina's
father Edward appearing to offer up a baby

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.780
to the Dark Lord.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:11.000
And crucially, in the background is what looks
like a nativity scene – the type you might

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.919
see in some Christian churches over Christmas
time.

00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:18.169
If that is a nativity scene behind Sabrina,
do the Three Demon Kings have something to

00:05:18.169 --> 00:05:20.389
do with what's going on in this scene?

00:05:20.389 --> 00:05:24.500
What's especially interesting is why this
scene was teased in the trailer but then never

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.780
appeared in the episode.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:30.009
Was it deleted or is it something that's going
to happen in a future episode of Season 2,

00:05:30.009 --> 00:05:31.040
for example the premiere?

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.860
Looking a bit more closely at what's going
on, I suspect this scene is a vision or dream

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:40.069
that Sabrina is having because she's wearing
a nightie and she isn't wearing her usual

00:05:40.069 --> 00:05:41.069
black hair-band.

00:05:41.069 --> 00:05:45.630
And I think it also relates back to that vision
Sabrina had in the very first episode of the

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:50.110
series where she saw her parents with a baby
in the woods and then she discovered a second

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.940
baby with cloven hooves.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:56.039
The baby that Edward is showing to the Dark
Lord is also wrapped in the same white crocheted

00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:58.310
fabric from Sabrina's Season 1 vision.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.390
Could this be another hint to an evil twin
for Sabrina in Season 2?

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:04.961
If you want to know more about that, then
tap the card here for my other video where

00:06:04.961 --> 00:06:08.650
I explain why Sabrina may have an evil twin
who she's yet to meet.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:12.090
I'll also add a link below in the video description
and at the end of this video.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:17.009
Fans of Michelle Gomez didn't get an awful
lot of the wicked demoness in the special

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:21.449
episode, but we do know that she still hasn't
received the promotion she was hoping for

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:22.720
from the Dark Lord.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:27.220
Obviously, she has plenty of trouble planned
for Sabrina in Season 2 and by the end of

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:31.920
this episode, in a deliciously wicked moment,
she takes a gingerbread version of Sabrina

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.789
and bites the head off, hinting at more voodoo
havoc in Season 2 which we also saw teased

00:06:36.789 --> 00:06:38.330
in the Part 2 trailer.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:43.521
In an interview with EW, showrunner Roberto
Aguirre-Sacasa has also revealed that, although

00:06:43.521 --> 00:06:48.479
Dr Cerberus didn't show up in this episode,
we're definitely going to find out what "secrets"

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:51.889
the bookstore owner "is keeping from [Aunt]
Hilda" in Part 2.

00:06:51.889 --> 00:06:57.130
I suspect Aguirre-Sacasa may be hinting at
Dr Cerberus's possible werewolf form teased

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.889
in the Season 2 trailer.

00:06:58.889 --> 00:07:03.729
Remember that in Season 1, Dr Cerberus said
that he's the oldest of three brothers; and,

00:07:03.729 --> 00:07:07.889
interestingly, in Greek mythology, Cerberus
is a multi-headed dog who keeps watch over

00:07:07.889 --> 00:07:09.319
the gates to the Underworld.

00:07:09.319 --> 00:07:14.169
Now, my question for you is do you think we'll
see more of Sabrina's mum Diana in Season

00:07:14.169 --> 00:07:15.169
2?

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:18.169
Let me know your thoughts and any other ideas
in the comments below.

